      "imageHeight": 4634,
      "story": "Simultaneous Contrasts is the title of a series of paintings created by Sonia Delaunay, beginning in 1912. The series was inspired by Eugène Chevreul's theory of simultaneous contrast, according to which the perception of color is affected by the presence of adjacent colors.",
